import tests/cadkernel/polyline_approximation3/main.dl

# The first source curve has already left scope through reassignment in the
# source fixture. Both approximations still own their independent point data.
check approximation3 (coarse's points != fine's points)
set copy to fine
set fine to a new (the type of fine)
check approximation3 copy's valid
check approximation3 ((the length of copy's points) > 2)
set point to the last item of (copy's points)
check approximation3 (((point's x = 4.0) and (point's y = 0.0)) and (point's z = 3.0))
set invalidCopy to refused
set refused to a new (the type of refused)
check approximation3 (invalidCopy's valid = false)

function approximation3 returned local result:
    execute:
        set points to a list containing the cad zero vector3
        append the cad x axis to points
        set values to an empty list of a 64 bit floating-point number
        set source to the cad nurbs curve3 of degree 1 with controls points, knots values and weights values
        free points
        free values
        return the cad spline polyline of source's value at precision 99
set retained to approximation3 returned local result
check approximation3 retained's valid
check approximation3 ((the length of retained's points) = 2)
set point to the last item of (retained's points)
check approximation3 (((point's x = 1.0) and (point's y = 0.0)) and (point's z = 0.0))
print "independent approximation buffers survive source and result reset" as a line
